            <persName type="full">Alfred Bergan</persName>
            <date type="birth" when="1879"/>
            <date type="death" when="1947-12-27"/>
            <note type="gender">M</note>
         </ab>
         <div type="bio">
            <p>A long-time friend of both JJ and his father, who spent time with both of them walking and socializing throughout Dublin. As an assistant to the sub-sheriff of Dublin, Bergan was in a position to be familiar with many people throughout the city and was known for his wit and playfulness. Following <name type="person" key="joyc49">John Joyce</name>’s death in December 1931, Bergan, as executor, corresponded frequently with JJ during 1932 to make burial arrangements. Bergan is one of few characters taken from historical Dublin to appear in <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Ulysses</name> under his own name, featuring prominently in the “Cyclops” episode as “Little Alf”. He was an important source for <name type="person" key="gorm93">Herbert Gorman</name>’s biography of JJ. <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
